# `movies/level29-firstaid.zmv` again with the fire button held, which is
# `tools/fit_route.py --fire`. The target is the same type-$14 object at
# (451,964) and the point is **how much health he has when he gets there.**
#
# Walking, he takes nineteen hits and arrives on six or less, so `$80:FACF` adds
# three and stores it. Shooting, he takes fifteen and arrives on seven, eight or
# nine -- and three would overshoot the ceiling of ten, so the entry clamps.
# **`heal_capped`** is the site for that clamp, it had been untaken by every
# input in the project, and this movie takes it five times while `heal_at_full`
# stays honestly at zero.
#
# It is also the movie with the most branch coverage of any single-player input:
# **51 of 111**, against 44 for the walking version. Firing turns on a whole
# subsystem the walking routes never touch -- `enemy_collide` runs 47 times here
# and 0 there.
#
# Both are kept. The walking route holds `victim_event_4`, `victim_ignore` and
# `victim_latched`, which nothing else reaches: a player who shoots his way
# across level 29 meets fewer neighbours than one who walks into them.
#
# `zamn_cosim verify -f 4250` checks 67,530 calls with no divergence.
#
# Twenty-three legs where the walking route took thirty-one, because `--fire` is
# free to the fitter: re-planning after every leg measures where the player *is*,
# so a shot that changes the board changes the next search's starting point and
# nothing else.

